   "text": "The hook is modeled in the project as design \"Under-desk headphone hook\", but the plan check did not fully pass, so I have stopped there.\n\nThe part is 40 x 30 x 40 mm: a 4 mm base plate, a 6 mm post and arm rising 40 mm, a 30 mm hook projection, rounded tip corners (10 mm radius), and two 4.5 mm screw holes at 24 mm spacing, each countersunk to 8.4 mm at 90 degrees. You said to use defaults, so every size is a guess and you should check them against your desk and screws before printing. The holes are vertical, so the hook prints plate-down and mounts upside down so it hangs below the desk.\n\nThe check flags three items, all from how the plan was written rather than the geometry. It counts each countersink as an extra 8.4 mm hole, and it counts the two countersinks as two features where the plan expected one step. The screw holes themselves measure correctly. I can't fix this without removing the countersinks, which the request needs.\n\nDo you want me to accept the model as it is (the countersinks count as intended), or change something first? Once you decide, I can set it up for the P1S in PLA and slice it. Sending it to the printer would need your approval."
